---
import PureRunLayout from '../../layouts/PureRunLayout.astro';
---

<PureRunLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — PureRun"
  description="PureRun’s privacy policy explains how the iPhone and Apple Watch apps use HealthKit without collecting or transmitting personal or health information."
  keywords="PureRun privacy policy, HealthKit privacy, Apple Watch running app, health data"
  current="privacy"
>
  <header class="bg-[#090b0d] px-6 py-20 text-center text-white sm:py-24">
    <p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#a7ff2f]">Private by construction</p>
    <h1 class="mt-5 text-5xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-6xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-gray-300">PureRun is designed so your running data never becomes our data.</p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-gray-500">Effective 1 August 2026</p>
  </header>

  <section class="bg-white py-20 dark:bg-gray-900 sm:py-24">
    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-gray mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 prose-headings:font-black prose-a:text-lime-700 dark:prose-invert dark:prose-a:text-[#a7ff2f] lg:px-8">
      <p class="lead">
        PureRun is a private running tracker for iPhone and Apple Watch. It has no account system, advertising, analytics, third-party SDK, or PureRun-operated server.
      </p>

      <h2>Health information</h2>
      <p>
        With your explicit permission, PureRun reads workouts, walking and running distance, heart rate, active energy, and running speed from Apple HealthKit. The Apple Watch app writes the running workouts you choose to record.
      </p>
      <p>
        PureRun uses this information only to record a run, display live workout metrics, show run history, and calculate your recent progress.
      </p>

      <h2>Data collection and sharing</h2>
      <p>
        PureRun does not collect, transmit, sell, rent, or disclose personal information or health information. Health information is processed on your devices and remains in HealthKit under Apple’s protection.
      </p>
      <p>
        PureRun does not use HealthKit information for advertising, marketing, profiling, data mining, insurance decisions, or research.
      </p>

      <h2>Local app information</h2>
      <p>
        Each device stores only a local preference indicating that first-run setup has been completed. PureRun does not copy your workout history into its own database.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention, deletion, and consent</h2>
      <p>
        Workout retention is controlled through Apple Health. You can delete workouts in the Health app and change or revoke PureRun’s Health permissions in the Health app or Settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        Removing PureRun deletes its local preferences. There is no PureRun account or server-held data to request or delete.
      </p>

      <h2>Apple services</h2>
      <p>
        HealthKit and any Health data synchronization are Apple services governed by your device, Apple Account, and iCloud settings. PureRun does not control or receive that synchronization.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially, the revised policy and its effective date will be published on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy or support questions, visit the <a href="/purerun/support">PureRun support page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#a7ff2f] px-6 py-14 text-center text-black">
    <p class="text-xl font-black">No account. No tracking. No PureRun server.</p>
    <a href="/purerun" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-bold underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Back to PureRun</a>
  </section>
</PureRunLayout>
